# Production build flags.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# ────────────────────
# `VITE_FILES_NATIVE` is inlined by vite AT BUILD TIME (see `NATIVE_FILES` in
# src/routes/report-view.tsx). It was previously passed on the command line,
# which means every `npm run build` that forgot it silently produced a bundle
# where the Files tab fell back to the framed Seafile UI — no error, no warning,
# just the old iframe where the native browser should be. That failure has now
# happened more than once, and a flag whose default is "quietly ship the thing we
# replaced" does not belong in someone's shell history.
#
# `.env.production` is loaded automatically by `npm run build` and is NOT
# gitignored (only `.env` and `.env.production.local` are), so the deployed
# default now lives with the code.
#
# `?files=frame` still forces the framed UI back for one session without a
# redeploy — URL beats build flag — so the rollback path is unchanged.
VITE_FILES_NATIVE="1"
